  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bridging the Gap: Gender Equality in the Commonwealth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The End-Term review of the previous Strategic Plan identified that a twin-track approach combining gender mainstreaming across all programmes with stand-alone initiatives on gender inclusion prove to be the most effective model for advancing gender equality. Stand-alone projects such as SheTrades and gender-responsive budgeting in small states, with their focus on results, member countries&apos; needs, and clear leadrship and accountability were found to generate sustainable policy impact. At the same time, embedding cross-cutting priorities into core programmes was found to be critical to ensure that gender mainstreaing is not treated as stand-alone issue but becomes part of the broader institutional agenda which leads to strengthening of gender inclusivity and legitimacy. Buildig on these lessons, advancing gender equality in this Strategic Plan will focus on (a) fostering even closer cooperation and further enhancing capacity of all programme teams to strengthen the integration of gender perspecives into conceptualisation, design, delivery, monitoring and evaluation of programmes and projects; (b) complementing this with stand-alone projects tht provide the dedicated attention, resources and innovation needed to address specific barriers and accelerate change. Together these mutually reinforcing strategies will promote both systemic transformation and targetted impact, leading to more sustainable and measurable progress towards gender equality across the three thematic pillars. COMSEC&apos;s comparative advantage which would be leveraged in this project includes; political convening power and trusted relationships across 56 member states (including SIDS/LDCs); thought leadership in gender equality; and cross sector technical expertise and South&#x2013;South peer learning to scale policy and practice rapidly and coherently.</narrative>
  </description>
